<title>UK: Newcastle Utd appoints banker with view to float.</title>
<headline>Newcastle Utd appoints banker with view to float.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>British soccer club  Newcastle United, currently leading the English Premier League, has appointed Mark Corbridge of investment bank NatWest Markets to advise on a floatation, the Times reported.</p>
<p>In its Friday edition, the paper says Corbridge has been appointed joint chief executive in charge of strategic development. Current chief executive Freddy Fletcher will remain in charge of the soccer businesses.</p>
<p>At five times turnover, Newcastle would be valued at around 200 million stg, the newspaper said and could be brought to market within the next few months.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
</text>
